"Federal Reserve Board - Survey of Consumer Finances (SCF) (https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/scfindex.htm)\nciteturn2view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/scfindex.htm\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 111\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】 【1†Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System The Federal Reserve, the central bank of the United States, provides the nation with a safe, flexible, and stable monetary and financial system.】\nL1: ## Survey of Consumer Finances (SCF)\nL2: \nL3: Please enable JavaScript if it is disabled in your browser or access the information through the links provided below.\nL4: \nL5: 【2†Current Survey】 【3†Codebook Search】【4†Documentation】【5†Previous Surveys】【6†Working Papers】【7†Confidential Data Access】【8†FAQs】【9†About】【10†Announcements】【11†Recent Changes】\nL6: The 2025 Survey of Consumer Finances (SCF) is the most recent survey conducted. Below are links to the report, interactive chartbook, historical report tables, full public dataset, extract dataset, replicate weight files, and technical documents.\nL7: #### Summary Results\nL8: \nL9: Changes in U.S. Family Finances from 2022 to 2025: Evidence from the Survey of Consumer Finances\nL10: 【12†PDF】\nL11: October 9, 2026\nL12: \nL13: 【13†Standard Error Tables (Excel)】\nL14: \nL15: 【14†Measuring Spending in the Survey of Consumer Finances】\nL16: \nL17: 【15†Informal Support Networks in the Survey of Consumer Finances】\nL18: \nL19: 【16†Heterogeneity in the Marginal Propensity to Consume among U.S. Households】\nL20: \nL21: #### SCF Interactive Chart\nL22: \nL23: 【17†View Interactive Chartbook】\nL24: \nL25: 【18†More information ​】\nL26: #### Historic Tables\nL27: \nL28: The following tables are based on those that have historically appeared in the main 【12†article】. Estimates for all survey years from 1989 to the most recent survey year are included in both nominal and real terms.\nL29: ##### Historic Tables Based on Internal and External Data\nL30: Historic Tables Based on Internal and External Data\nL31: File Type  | File  | Documentation  | Last Updated\nL32: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL33: Excel Based on Internal Data  | 【19†Estimates in nominal dollars (2 MB Excel)】\nL34: 【20†Estimates inflation-adjusted to 2025 dollars (3 MB Excel)】  | 【21†Summary Extract Data Program (TXT)】  | 10/9/2026\nL35: Excel Based on Public Data  | 【22†Estimates in nominal dollars (3 MB Excel)】\nL36: 【23†Estimates inflation-adjusted to 2025 dollars (3 MB Excel)】  | 10/9/2026\nL37: \nL38: 【24†More information ​】\nL39: #### Survey Data and Replicate Weight Files\nL40: ##### Full Public Data Set - Full data sets of all SCF variables.\nL41: Full Public Data Set Files by Format\nL42: File Type  | Main Survey Data  | Replicate Weight File (X42001)  | Documentation  | Last Updated\nL43: --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nL44: SAS  | 【25†CPORT version (10 MB ZIP)】\nL45: 【26†COPY/EXPORT version (15 MB ZIP)】  | 【27†CPORT version (27 MB ZIP)】\nL46: 【28†COPY/EXPORT version (27 MB ZIP)】  | 【29†Codebook (2.7 MB ASCII)】 【30†Standard Error Documentation (PDF)】 【31†Changes for 2025 (PDF)】  | 10/9/2026\nL47: STATA  | 【32†Stata version (9 MB ZIP)】  | 【33†Stata version (26 MB ZIP)】  | 10/9/2026\nL48: ASCII  | 【34†ASCII (38 MB ZIP)】\nL49: 【35†Variable Map: Excel (Excel)】\nL50: 【36†Variable Map: Tab-delimited (ASCII)】  |    | 10/9/2026\nL51: WARNING: Please review the following 【30†PDF】 for instructions on how to calculate correct standard errors. As a result of multiple imputation, the dataset you are downloading contains five times the number of actual observations. Failure to account for the imputations and the complex sample design will result in incorrect estimation of standard errors.\nL52: \nL53: 【37†More information ​】\nL54: Special note to R users: An outside programmer has created scripts for converting and working with SCF data. These scripts are available for download from: 【38†https://guilhermejacob.github.io/context/1.6-survey-of-consumer-finances-scf.html#survey-of-consumer-finances-scf†guilhermejacob.github.io】\nL55: ##### Summary Extract Public Data - Summary variables used in the 【39†Federal Reserve Report】 – all dollar variables inflation-adjusted to 2025 dollars.\nL56: Summary Extract Public Data Files by Format\nL57: File Type  | File  | Documentation  | Last Updated\nL58: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL59: SDA online analysis  | 【40†SDA analysis tool†sda.berkeley.edu】  | 【41†Creating SCF Bulletin Tables in SDA (DOC】) 【21†SAS macro - Variable Definitions (TXT)】      | 10/9/2026\nL60: SAS  | 【42†SAS extract data (3 MB ZIP)】  | 10/9/2026\nL61: STATA  | 【43†Stata extract data (3 MB ZIP)】  | 10/9/2026\nL62: CSV  | 【44†CSV extract data (2 MB ZIP)】  | 10/9/2026\nL63: \nL64: 【45†More information ​】\nL65: #### Technical Documents\nL66: \nL67: Technical Documentation Files\nL68: File  | Last Updated\nL69: --- | ---\nL70: 【29†Codebook (2.7 MB ASCII)】  | 10/9/2026\nL71: 【46†Showcards (PDF)】  | 10/9/2026\nL72: 【47†Questionnaire Outline (PDF)】  | 10/9/2026\nL73: 【48†Simulation of MR Interview Program (1 MB DOCX)】  | 10/9/2026\nL74: 【31†Changes for 2025 (PDF)】  | 10/9/2026\nL75: 【49†Net Worth Flowchart (PDF)】  | 10/9/2026\nL76: \nL77: 【50†More information ​】\nL78: #### Missing Data\nL79: Missing data in the survey have been imputed five times using a multiple imputation technique. The information is stored in five separate imputation replicates (implicates). Thus, for the 4,367 families interviewed for the survey, there are 21,835 records in the data set. Seven observations were deleted for the public version of the data set for purposes of disclosure avoidance; thus, there are 21,800 records in the public data set for 4,360 families.\nL80: The codebook provides more detail on the structure of the data set and the steps taken for disclosure avoidance.\nL81: 【51†Back to Top】\nL82: \nL83: Last Update: 10/09/2026\nL84: ###### Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System